      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 4861,
      "endIndex": 4979,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "High-quality cotton is easy to maintain, but a little extra care will keep your garments looking brand new for years.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00064",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[64]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 4979,
      "endIndex": 4980,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00065",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[65]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 4980,
      "endIndex": 5155,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "1. Wash in Cold Water: Always wash your cotton clothes in cold water. Hot water can break down natural cotton fibers over time and lead to unwanted shrinkage or color fading.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00066",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[66]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5155,
      "endIndex": 5337,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "2. Turn Garments Inside Out: To protect the outer finish and color brightness of your clothes, turn shirts, tees, and trousers inside out before putting them in the washing machine.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00067",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[67]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5337,
      "endIndex": 5495,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "3. Use Gentle Detergents: Avoid harsh bleaches or heavy chemical detergents, especially on organic cotton. A mild detergent keeps the fibers soft and strong.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00068",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[68]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5495,
      "endIndex": 5693,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "4. Air Dry in the Shade: High heat from tumble dryers is the enemy of natural fibers. Hang your cotton clothes outside to line-dry in the shade to prevent shrinkage and maintain their original fit.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
